{"availability":"available","full":"BandarLabs/Cobalt","name":"Cobalt","description":"SDK for building apps & an app store for your Kobo eInk reader","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":393,"forks":42,"created":"2026-07-29T15:06:20Z","updated":"2026-10-11T13:39:58Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bandarlabs.github.io/Cobalt/","topics":["arxiv","eink","epub","epub-reader","ereader","kobo","kobo-ereader","lichess","opds-client","rss-reader","sdk","syncthing","wallabag","zotero"],"demo":"https://bandarlabs.github.io/Cobalt/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:43:11.293Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T09:43:11.293Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T09:43:11.293Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:11.837Z","stars":383,"forks":41},{"at":"2026-10-09T08:56:05.491Z","stars":385,"forks":42},{"at":"2026-10-12T09:43:11.293Z","stars":393,"forks":42}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Cobalt adds apps to Kobo e-readers. It includes a launcher, an app store, a Rust SDK, a runtime that runs each app in its own restricted process, and a simulator for building apps without a device.","Tested on the Kobo Clara BW (N365 and the 2025 P365), Clara Colour, Clara HD, Elipsa 2E, Libra 2, Libra Colour and Libra H2O, at the firmware listed in the device support matrix. Other Kobos can run it too: Cobalt lists what has not been tested and asks once before it starts. Kobo firmware 5.x is not supported. Cobalt is not affiliated with Rakuten Kobo."],"features":["Signed app installs, updates and removal over Wi-Fi.","App pages on the website that install to a linked Kobo by QR code or pairing","Every app runs in its own unprivileged process, and must declare the","services it uses, such as network, storage, audio or the front light.","Cobalt updates are separate from app updates."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BandarLabs/Cobalt/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bccb1bb4a05b1d760